        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: align iOS icons with favicon mark",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where the iOS app icon assets still used the older lobster silhouette while the OpenClaw app UI and web favicon use the newer rounded OpenClaw favicon mark from `ui/public/favicon.svg`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRegenerated the iOS production/debug app icon sets, the embedded watch idiom icons, the Watch app production/debug icon sets, and the Watch fallback `OpenClawIcon` raster image from the canonical favicon SVG. App icon rasters are flattened to opaque PNGs for Apple asset-catalog requirements; the Watch in-app fallback image keeps transparency for circular UI use.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers see the same OpenClaw favicon mascot across the iOS app icon, debug app icon, Watch companion icons, and Watch fallback avatar instead of a mix of old and new logo treatments.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, generated with Codex.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Source image verified from `https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/ui/public/favicon.svg`.\n- Swept iOS logo/image surfaces with `rg` and `git ls-files`; touched all 85 tracked PNG assets under `apps/ios`.\n- Verified all app-icon PNGs retain their expected dimensions and have no alpha via `sips -g pixelWidth -g pixelHeight -g hasAlpha`.\n- Verified `apps/ios/WatchApp/Assets.xcassets/OpenClawIcon.imageset/openclaw-icon.png` remains 180x180 with alpha for in-app circular rendering.\n- Ran `git diff --check`.\n- Ran `pnpm ios:gen`.\n- Ran `pnpm ios:build` successfully for `OpenClaw` on `platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17`.\n\nNote: `codex --version` failed locally because the installed CLI points at a missing vendor binary (`ENOENT`), so `codex review --base origin/main` could not be run in this environment.\n",
